177 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(DALL.E mini was released as an open-access version of its bigger sibling, DALL.E 1 \(which was publicly unavailable at the time\). While this model lacked precision and often included distorted features, it showcased the early potential of AI to bring imagination to life. )/Pg 13 0 R/K[4]/P 75 0 R>>
endobj

178 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Two years later, DALL\267E 3 transformed the game with a focus on detail, coherence, and contextual understanding. Unlike DALLE mini, DALL\267E 3 mastered complex scenes and produced exceptional realism and accurate images. It incorporated better alignment with user intent and reduced odd or unintended outputs. )/Pg 13 0 R/K[5]/P 75 0 R>>
endobj

