207 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(With OpenAI's plans to release its first operator soon, Google Deepmind is already one step ahead with its project Mariner, powered by the new Gemini 3 model. Although in a state of limited access, Project Mariner enables AI systems to assist users in web-based interaction through tasks such as research, booking flights, and shopping. )/Pg 15 0 R/K[0]/P 77 0 R>>
endobj

208 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Project Mariner appears as a chat window on the right side of your browser. It accompanies you in searching the web and breaks down complex steps into simple steps for the user. Google's Mariner works by sending screenshots of your browser window to the Gemini 2 model for processing. )/Pg 15 0 R/K[1]/P 77 0 R>>
endobj

209 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Project Mariner is still in its developmental stages with much of its potential yet to be realised. Google Deepmind's Gemini has been prone to hallucinations \(for information on hallucination, see page _\), and AI malfunction on a larger scale as Project Mariner could be disastrous. Thus, more time is required to prevent critical errors. For example, if a user asks the model to buy an item or book a holiday, the model could unknowingly enter personal information on a malicious website that appears similar \(and using AI has been fine-tuned to appear on AGI user prompts\), compromising personal data. )/Pg 15 0 R/K[2]/P 77 0 R>>
endobj

210 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Now scale this scenario to 275 million users per month \(current monthly Gemini users\) who could potentially come into contact with this website, and it's easy to see the issues that could arise. Safety concerns like these are why it is taking so long for AGI to be introduced. )/Pg 15 0 R/K[3]/P 77 0 R>>
endobj

211 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(PROJECT MARINER: GOOGLE'S AMBITIOUS AGI ENDEAVOR)/E(PROJECT MARINER: GOOGLE'S AMBITIOUS AGI ENDEAVOR)/Pg 15 0 R/K[4]/P 77 0 R>>
endobj

