322 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Do machines truly have the ability to 'learn,' or do they mimic our behaviour? As AI evolves, it has sparked comparisons to human cognition, but how far does this parallel go?)/Alt()/Pg 25 0 R/K[0]/P 87 0 R>>
endobj

323 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Humans don't just solve problems; we generate meaning with acts and intent based on prior experience, going through trial and error and drawing connections with our lived experience and conscience. )/Alt()/Pg 25 0 R/K[1]/P 87 0 R>>
endobj

324 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Contrarily, AI recognises patterns and makes predictions for an outcome similar to humans, going through trial and error, albeit systematically. )/Alt()/Pg 25 0 R/K[2]/P 87 0 R>>
endobj

325 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(What differs, however, is creativity. AI has no prior lived experience as humans do; its version of 'creativity' is created through pattern recognition based on its training; no abstract thinking is involved, which is a fundamental requirement through creativity. )/Alt()/Pg 25 0 R/K[3]/P 87 0 R>>
endobj

326 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(Similarly, AI can mimic human emotion, primarily to enhance communication, but it doesn't understand human thought or emotional logic. Without culture or experience, there is no foundation for genuine emotion.)/Alt()/Pg 25 0 R/K[4]/P 87 0 R>>
endobj

327 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(These factors are the most noticeable missing features of AI compared to humans, but with AI's rapid growth, it is likely a matter of when, not if, AI can showcase these things.)/Alt()/Pg 25 0 R/K[5]/P 87 0 R>>
endobj

328 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(The expansion of this technology raises questions that no one can truly answer, such as: When an AI expresses an emotion that deviates from its programming, is it truly feeling or simply mimicking?)/Alt()/Pg 25 0 R/K[6]/P 87 0 R>>
endobj

